WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.875 --> 00:00:04.792
(ambient noises from outdoors)

00:00:05.890 --> 00:00:07.960
- [Mark] All right, Rita.

00:00:07.960 --> 00:00:08.820
Welcome back.

00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:10.500
- [Rita] Hi, I guess.

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:12.840
- [Mark] So, you were
just telling me outside

00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:16.030
that you actually prefer
to be living on the street

00:00:16.030 --> 00:00:17.330
than in the hospital that you were in?

00:00:17.330 --> 00:00:20.430
- I don't wanna go back to the hospital.

00:00:20.430 --> 00:00:22.430
I don't want them to tell me what to do,

00:00:22.430 --> 00:00:24.170
and they don't give you seconds

00:00:24.170 --> 00:00:26.740
when they give you your medication,

00:00:26.740 --> 00:00:28.780
and I be hungry when I get up.

00:00:28.780 --> 00:00:32.660
And what's important to me is
I wanna be like these ladies

00:00:32.660 --> 00:00:36.180
that have nice clothes and look nice.

00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:41.180
But I went to visit a friend,
and I wanted some food,

00:00:41.540 --> 00:00:44.679
and they had a lot left
and they threw it away

00:00:44.679 --> 00:00:49.500
because in the Allison,
the security said I'm nasty

00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:53.320
and I got a disease, and I got AIDS,

00:00:53.320 --> 00:00:56.290
and they don't want me in they building

00:00:56.290 --> 00:00:58.620
'cause I'm nasty and ugly.

00:00:58.620 --> 00:01:02.640
And they be havin', all the
other securities have meetings

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:06.730
about me and don't nobody
like me because I'm retarded.

00:01:06.730 --> 00:01:08.790
And I said, "I'm special."

00:01:08.790 --> 00:01:10.800
And they said they don't want nobody

00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:15.800
who can't read and write
'cause they retarded and dirty.

00:01:17.305 --> 00:01:18.261
And my mama (crosstalk)--

00:01:18.261 --> 00:01:19.797
- [Mark] They didn't feed you?

00:01:19.797 --> 00:01:22.600
- And they threw all
the food away right now.

00:01:22.600 --> 00:01:27.600
And I almost was cryin' because
they gave a girl some food

00:01:29.150 --> 00:01:32.840
that I be visitin' and
they had a lot of food

00:01:32.840 --> 00:01:35.640
and they wouldn't even let me
get none out the garbage can,

00:01:35.640 --> 00:01:37.573
they told me to get back.

00:01:39.210 --> 00:01:42.251
They don't like me, and
I didn't do nothin'.

00:01:42.251 --> 00:01:44.210
- [Mark] So, you actually prefer,

00:01:44.210 --> 00:01:45.270
I mean, you live on the street,

00:01:45.270 --> 00:01:46.610
you don't even have a tent, right?

00:01:46.610 --> 00:01:47.867
- No, I don't wanna be by my...

00:01:47.867 --> 00:01:52.867
I wanna be by myself, I don't
wanna be with nobody 'cause--

00:01:53.395 --> 00:01:54.228
- [Mark] What's wrong with the hospital?

00:01:54.228 --> 00:01:55.470
- Only my mama.

00:01:55.470 --> 00:01:59.620
At the hospital, they keep
you locked up in a room

00:01:59.620 --> 00:02:04.620
and you eat in a hall, and
they give me medication,

00:02:04.950 --> 00:02:09.020
but when they give me food,
lunch and breakfast and stuff,

00:02:09.020 --> 00:02:10.693
they don't give me seconds.

00:02:13.246 --> 00:02:16.040
- [Mark] What does your
typical day look like

00:02:16.040 --> 00:02:17.690
here living in Skid Row?

00:02:17.690 --> 00:02:20.270
- I just wanna be like my friend,

00:02:20.270 --> 00:02:23.180
she take me to her house
and give me clothes

00:02:23.180 --> 00:02:27.851
but she makes me, she tell
me to go make some money

00:02:27.851 --> 00:02:31.320
and pay for her clothes
because she doin' it

00:02:31.320 --> 00:02:34.173
'cause I'm her friend
but she need help too.

00:02:36.240 --> 00:02:37.580
- [Mark] So your typical day here

00:02:37.580 --> 00:02:40.180
on the street is what, what do you do?

00:02:40.180 --> 00:02:45.180
- I walk around and I just be happy.

00:02:46.300 --> 00:02:50.080
I talk to my mother too, my
mother said she's coming back.

00:02:50.080 --> 00:02:52.173
My mama said she's gone come back.

00:02:53.760 --> 00:02:56.750
My mother tell me and
God, my mother tell me

00:02:56.750 --> 00:03:01.040
to just stay to myself, and then she...

00:03:01.040 --> 00:03:06.040
I go and sit on the corner,
and then a man stops sometimes,

00:03:06.304 --> 00:03:10.570
they look at my body, they give me money,

00:03:10.570 --> 00:03:12.800
and they take me to eat.

00:03:12.800 --> 00:03:14.560
(interviewer sighs)

00:03:14.560 --> 00:03:15.970
- [Mark] So people are
nice to you on the street,

00:03:15.970 --> 00:03:17.720
or mean to you or little
bit of (crosstalk)?

00:03:17.720 --> 00:03:22.310
- Some peoples is nice but
I just wanna be by myself

00:03:22.310 --> 00:03:24.950
'cause when they nice,
I gotta give them money

00:03:24.950 --> 00:03:27.282
when I don't feel like givin' 'em.

00:03:27.282 --> 00:03:30.020
Makin' money, I just feel like just peace,

00:03:30.020 --> 00:03:32.050
me and God and my mother,

00:03:32.050 --> 00:03:35.927
but I have to or I can't be on the street.

00:03:35.927 --> 00:03:38.000
- [Mark] Do you get robbed sometimes?

00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:38.833
- Huh?

00:03:38.833 --> 00:03:40.400
- [Mark] Have you been robbed a few times?

00:03:40.400 --> 00:03:43.190
- No, I give it to 'em if they tell me to.

00:03:43.190 --> 00:03:44.603
- [Mark] Oh, I see.

00:03:46.380 --> 00:03:50.370
- I share anything I got because God said

00:03:50.370 --> 00:03:51.883
you gotta share a blessing.

00:03:53.030 --> 00:03:57.377
But only thing happened to me
is I give my sugar boat to--

00:03:58.490 --> 00:03:59.323
- [Mark] Your what?

00:03:59.323 --> 00:04:04.323
- They take my sugar boat
down there, a lot o' times.

00:04:04.430 --> 00:04:05.263
- [Mark] They take your what?

00:04:05.263 --> 00:04:07.510
- Sugar boat, they give me, you know,

00:04:07.510 --> 00:04:10.970
sometimes on this street,
they give me rocks,

00:04:10.970 --> 00:04:12.500
and then they say, "Let's party,

00:04:12.500 --> 00:04:14.030
I don't want nuttin' from you."

00:04:14.030 --> 00:04:17.190
And then when I party, I
gotta give 'em my body.

00:04:17.190 --> 00:04:18.300
- [Mark] (softly) Oh, I see.

00:04:18.300 --> 00:04:23.300
- And then I just do it so they
won't kill me and my money.

00:04:26.330 --> 00:04:27.250
- [Mark] And yet you still prefer

00:04:27.250 --> 00:04:29.150
to live on the street
than in the hospital?

00:04:29.150 --> 00:04:31.343
- Yeah, because nobody like me.

00:04:32.560 --> 00:04:34.540
- [Mark] So Rita, tell me
about your mom and dad.

00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:38.160
- My mom and dad, when I was young,

00:04:38.160 --> 00:04:42.850
my dad and mom get drunk,
he used to drown my mom

00:04:42.850 --> 00:04:45.830
in a bathtub and put the water on,

00:04:45.830 --> 00:04:50.570
and make it real, real
hot, and she'd be screamin'

00:04:50.570 --> 00:04:53.230
and then I'll hold her hand
and tell her it's okay,

00:04:53.230 --> 00:04:56.070
he tell me to shut up, and I go in there

00:04:56.070 --> 00:04:58.950
and run out the bathroom and get a broom

00:04:58.950 --> 00:05:01.383
and hit 'im in the back
o' his head and stuff.

00:05:02.494 --> 00:05:04.840
And he'd run after me, my mom'd hurry up

00:05:04.840 --> 00:05:07.970
and get out the bathtub
and run out the door

00:05:07.970 --> 00:05:10.230
and go call the police.

00:05:10.230 --> 00:05:14.073
My dad, when they not drinkin',

00:05:14.073 --> 00:05:17.470
he don't got time for my mom.

00:05:17.470 --> 00:05:20.560
My mom said that's not my
dad, they were just young

00:05:20.560 --> 00:05:23.220
and partyin' and she got pregnant by 'im,

00:05:23.220 --> 00:05:25.280
but she wanted us to know our dad.

00:05:25.280 --> 00:05:29.170
But he tried to kill her a lot o' times.

00:05:29.170 --> 00:05:31.710
And I run in a closet and cover up

00:05:31.710 --> 00:05:33.653
with some clothes on my head.

00:05:34.630 --> 00:05:37.210
And I'd be scared and run in a closet,

00:05:37.210 --> 00:05:39.800
shut the closet, cover my head up,

00:05:39.800 --> 00:05:41.403
'cause I don't wanna see it.

00:05:42.528 --> 00:05:46.870
And then when he make
my mom bloody, he leave,

00:05:46.870 --> 00:05:49.370
she hurried and lock the
door and come and get me,

00:05:50.660 --> 00:05:53.223
and rocked me while she
cleanin' herself up.

00:05:55.190 --> 00:05:58.223
I still be with my mom, I love my mom.

00:05:59.540 --> 00:06:01.630
'Cause my sister live in Sacramento,

00:06:01.630 --> 00:06:03.703
she call me "retarded" too.

00:06:04.550 --> 00:06:08.133
And she don't want my
nieces and 'em around me,

00:06:10.400 --> 00:06:12.920
'cause they say I'm
wearin' the same clothes

00:06:12.920 --> 00:06:16.950
I got the virus, and
I'm ugly and retarded,

00:06:16.950 --> 00:06:20.070
and she made 'em leave me alone.

00:06:20.070 --> 00:06:23.587
But I go to the Union
Station, and they help me

00:06:23.587 --> 00:06:27.630
and I give it to her,
so I wouldn't be cold.

00:06:27.630 --> 00:06:30.817
Only when it's cold and
rainin', I could stay with her.

00:06:31.730 --> 00:06:32.563
- [Mark] I think you're wearing

00:06:32.563 --> 00:06:33.760
the same clothes as last time.

00:06:33.760 --> 00:06:35.666
- Yeah, 'cause I couldn't get none.

00:06:35.666 --> 00:06:38.480
With the money, I gave her some,

00:06:38.480 --> 00:06:42.380
and then I bought some food for her house.

00:06:42.380 --> 00:06:44.543
And then I bought some rock.

00:06:46.000 --> 00:06:47.676
But I bought food first--

00:06:47.676 --> 00:06:48.560
- [Mark] You say you brought rock--

00:06:48.560 --> 00:06:49.940
- Yeah, I gave her some.

00:06:49.940 --> 00:06:50.970
- [Mark] You mean crack.

00:06:50.970 --> 00:06:52.750
- Well yeah, I didn't buy it,

00:06:52.750 --> 00:06:55.451
I give her some money, her give me some.

00:06:55.451 --> 00:06:56.440
- [Mark] 'Kay.

00:06:56.440 --> 00:06:58.350
- But I take everything to her,

00:06:58.350 --> 00:07:03.350
unless'n I just go and
buy the stuff, food first.

00:07:03.820 --> 00:07:07.210
I don't buy drugs 'cause
they takes my money.

00:07:07.210 --> 00:07:11.313
I don't buy drugs, I let
somebody give it to me or buy it.

00:07:13.150 --> 00:07:15.400
'Cause I'm scared, you know,

00:07:15.400 --> 00:07:18.493
mostly my peoples, they don't like me.

00:07:19.920 --> 00:07:23.480
Last night, security, he was callin' me

00:07:23.480 --> 00:07:26.720
all kinds a nasty A- prostitute,

00:07:26.720 --> 00:07:30.930
and said all of the securities
be laughin' every day

00:07:30.930 --> 00:07:33.530
and talkin' about me and havin' a meeting

00:07:33.530 --> 00:07:35.680
of how retarded I am.

00:07:35.680 --> 00:07:40.470
And that's sad, and then I'm
not good like these people

00:07:40.470 --> 00:07:45.470
and my mother told me I was
just special and different,

00:07:45.650 --> 00:07:48.380
but they say that I'm retarded,

00:07:48.380 --> 00:07:51.773
to be around them I need
to learn how to read,

00:07:54.000 --> 00:07:57.640
and to dress better than I do.

00:07:57.640 --> 00:08:00.080
- [Mark] Oh, you dress beautifully.

00:08:00.080 --> 00:08:04.420
- It's clean, but she...

00:08:04.420 --> 00:08:07.610
The lady who was here,
she don't wanna give me

00:08:07.610 --> 00:08:09.580
no more o' her clothes.

00:08:09.580 --> 00:08:10.413
- [Mark] Are you cold at night?

00:08:10.413 --> 00:08:11.900
- She gave me this...

00:08:11.900 --> 00:08:13.184
Is I'm cold (crosstalk)?

00:08:13.184 --> 00:08:17.820
Yeah, but I get on the
train, when it's real cold,

00:08:17.820 --> 00:08:21.770
I get on the train, and at
her house I got a medication.

00:08:21.770 --> 00:08:25.710
I got a pump and a machine, and inhaler.

00:08:27.260 --> 00:08:30.140
I got a gray one and a orange one.

00:08:30.140 --> 00:08:30.980
- [Mark] Could I buy you a jacket?

00:08:30.980 --> 00:08:32.310
- I got...

00:08:32.310 --> 00:08:33.940
Yeah, you got a jacket?

00:08:33.940 --> 00:08:34.773
- [Mark] Yeah, I'll--

00:08:34.773 --> 00:08:38.178
- 'Cause a man, he gave me that jacket.

00:08:38.178 --> 00:08:41.123
He had it on layin' on the ground,

00:08:41.123 --> 00:08:43.042
and he gave it to me last night.

00:08:43.042 --> 00:08:43.875
- [Mark] Okay, well I
can give you something

00:08:43.875 --> 00:08:45.000
a little warmer maybe.

00:08:45.000 --> 00:08:46.140
- Okay.

00:08:46.140 --> 00:08:47.570
- [Mark] Where do you normally sleep?

00:08:47.570 --> 00:08:48.403
- Me?

00:08:48.403 --> 00:08:49.236
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:08:49.236 --> 00:08:51.363
- At the mostly, 'cause when I'm scared,

00:08:53.090 --> 00:08:56.870
'cause if one person tell
me that they want my body

00:08:56.870 --> 00:08:58.587
and I ain't got it, if
I got money, I'd say,

00:08:58.587 --> 00:09:01.290
"I'll give you some money, but
please don't take my body."

00:09:01.290 --> 00:09:04.160
And then I'd just go
catch the bus real fast

00:09:04.160 --> 00:09:05.427
when I give 'em the money and say,

00:09:05.427 --> 00:09:08.160
"I'mma go somewhere to me
somethin' to snack on."

00:09:08.160 --> 00:09:10.299
I'd tell a story and I'd get on the bus,

00:09:10.299 --> 00:09:11.710
and go to train station.

00:09:11.710 --> 00:09:12.710
- [Mark] And you don't get money

00:09:12.710 --> 00:09:16.430
from Social Security or any like that?

00:09:16.430 --> 00:09:17.263
- No, sir.

00:09:18.380 --> 00:09:19.984
- [Mark] So every dollar that you--

00:09:19.984 --> 00:09:22.543
- I got the letter and anything

00:09:22.543 --> 00:09:25.130
that they's gonna help me, so...

00:09:25.130 --> 00:09:26.530
- [Mark] But right now,
the only money that you get

00:09:26.530 --> 00:09:28.160
is from the money you make on the street?

00:09:28.160 --> 00:09:28.993
- Yeah.

00:09:29.860 --> 00:09:31.810
I ask for donations.

00:09:31.810 --> 00:09:34.110
People at the grocery store give me food,

00:09:34.110 --> 00:09:36.550
then I take it to her,
so we could share it.

00:09:36.550 --> 00:09:39.680
But she my best friend,
she try to help me.

00:09:39.680 --> 00:09:44.026
And then we play a little
game of alphabets and stuff...

00:09:44.026 --> 00:09:45.463
(people faintly talking in the background)

00:09:45.463 --> 00:09:47.319
Like a puzzle.

00:09:47.319 --> 00:09:48.490
- [Mark] All right, Rita, well I'm gonna,

00:09:48.490 --> 00:09:50.730
I'm gonna make your day a
little easier, at least.

00:09:50.730 --> 00:09:51.947
(Rita mumbles softly)

00:09:51.947 --> 00:09:53.340
(sighs) Well thank you
for coming in again.

00:09:53.340 --> 00:09:56.274
- Yeah, you got some food here?

00:09:56.274 --> 00:09:57.230
- [Mark] I have some money for ya.

00:09:57.230 --> 00:09:58.398
I'll set you up with some food (chuckles).

00:09:58.398 --> 00:09:59.231
- Okay, all right.

00:09:59.231 --> 00:10:00.210
- [Mark] You can go
anywhere you like for lunch.

00:10:00.210 --> 00:10:02.260
- Okay, I'mma go cross the street.

00:10:02.260 --> 00:10:03.093
- [Mark] Excellent.

00:10:03.093 --> 00:10:05.870
- The Mexicans and the Caucasian guy,

00:10:05.870 --> 00:10:10.650
'cause I got a stepdad,
he's a truck driver,

00:10:10.650 --> 00:10:14.780
but he live in Big Bear, and
he only come once a month.

00:10:14.780 --> 00:10:19.360
His name is (name muted) and
since I came to California '98,

00:10:19.360 --> 00:10:22.250
he take care o' me, but he don't no more

00:10:22.250 --> 00:10:25.940
because they told 'im that I can't ride

00:10:25.940 --> 00:10:28.780
with him on the road, and
it's too far for him to come.

00:10:28.780 --> 00:10:29.613
- [Mark] Hmm.

00:10:31.216 --> 00:10:32.049
- [Rita] But yeah--

00:10:32.049 --> 00:10:32.882
- [Mark] A'right well, if
you ever get into a jam,

00:10:32.882 --> 00:10:33.715
you come see me, okay?

00:10:33.715 --> 00:10:34.548
- [Rita] Okay.

00:10:34.548 --> 00:10:35.440
- [Mark] If you ever
need help with anything.

00:10:35.440 --> 00:10:36.273
- [Rita] Yeah.

00:10:36.273 --> 00:10:37.106
- [Mark] Excellent.

00:10:37.106 --> 00:10:38.028
- [Rita] Yeah.

00:10:38.028 --> 00:10:39.030
- [Mark] A'right Rita, well
thank you for coming in.

00:10:39.030 --> 00:10:40.263
- [Rita] Thank you, you welcome.

00:10:40.263 --> 00:10:41.271
- [Mark] It's great to see you again.

00:10:41.271 --> 00:10:42.104
- [Rita] Yes.

00:10:42.104 --> 00:10:43.268
Am I a movie star?

00:10:43.268 --> 00:10:44.101
(interviewer laughs)

00:10:44.101 --> 00:10:46.570
I told the people that I'm a movie star.

00:10:46.570 --> 00:10:47.700
- [Mark] (laughs) You are a movie star.

00:10:47.700 --> 00:10:51.250
- [Rita] 'Cause they put
some wires and stuff.

00:10:51.250 --> 00:10:52.458
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:10:52.458 --> 00:10:53.291
- [Rita] (voice becoming
distant) Well, you know...

00:10:53.291 --> 00:10:54.420
Uh-oh, I got this (removing
sound equipment)...

00:10:54.420 --> 00:10:57.697
I wanted to be on Dancing With the Stars,

00:10:57.697 --> 00:11:00.079
but I came here and my (voice fades out).

00:11:00.079 --> 00:11:01.455
- [Woman] (voice fading
in) Some more food.

00:11:01.455 --> 00:11:02.288
- [Mark] Who's that?

00:11:02.288 --> 00:11:03.121
- Rita Calvin!

00:11:03.121 --> 00:11:03.995
- [Mark] Hey, what'd ya got?

00:11:03.995 --> 00:11:06.077
- And he bought me some clothes!

00:11:06.077 --> 00:11:09.960
And I got a skirt too, a go-go skirt.

00:11:09.960 --> 00:11:12.187
And I got some tennis shoes.

00:11:12.187 --> 00:11:14.700
(interviewer chuckles)

00:11:14.700 --> 00:11:19.700
God sent my friend in my life,
I got a lotta pretty clothes,

00:11:20.430 --> 00:11:22.690
over there on Los Angeles Street.

00:11:22.690 --> 00:11:23.901
- [Mark] But, with the money I gave you?

00:11:23.901 --> 00:11:24.734
- Yes!

00:11:24.734 --> 00:11:25.793
- [Mark] Oh, I see, okay.

00:11:25.793 --> 00:11:27.319
- I went shop, I came back--

00:11:27.319 --> 00:11:28.152
- [Mark] Look at you, you look beautiful.

00:11:28.152 --> 00:11:31.536
- Thank you, I came back to
show you, but you wasn't here.

00:11:31.536 --> 00:11:32.369
- [Mark] Oh, I'm here today.

00:11:32.369 --> 00:11:34.850
- I got some tennis shoes,
socks, and a skirt--

00:11:34.850 --> 00:11:35.715
- [Mark] You look so stylish.

00:11:35.715 --> 00:11:36.548
- And a shirt--

00:11:36.548 --> 00:11:37.381
- [Mark] You're beautiful.

00:11:37.381 --> 00:11:40.540
- Thank you, so I'm
lookin' cute like them now.

00:11:40.540 --> 00:11:41.570
- [Mark] Yeah, you look
cuter than they do.

00:11:41.570 --> 00:11:43.610
You look great (crosstalk).

00:11:43.610 --> 00:11:44.443
All right, darlin'.

